# The ledger of `containers/cache`: the cache that forgets the entry used
# least recently, with a time to live. Python 3.15's `functools.lru_cache` and
# `functools.cache` are the three libraries' only ones; Java's `LinkedHashMap`
# in access order is named in the notes.
#
# A record takes no type parameter, so a cache is a shape beside the
# program's own key list, value list and `{K: i64}` lookup map, lent with `@`.

## The cache

capability cache/make  a cache of a capacity, with a time to live or none
  heroes  cache.new, cache.new_with_ttl, cache.capacity
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  functools.lru_cache, functools.cache
  note    time is the program's: every call that can expire takes `now` in the program's own unit and no clock is read, so a test needs none, and the package needs no `time`, whose use adds 2,098,016 bytes to a program (309,368 against 2,407,384, measured 2026-11-17). Python's `lru_cache` wraps a function; the function here is the program's, which asks `cache.get` and on `not_found` computes and calls `cache.put`. Java's LinkedHashMap in access order with `removeEldestEntry` is this

capability cache/put  a value put, the least recently used forgotten where the cache is full
  heroes  cache.put
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the expired entries are forgotten first; checked against a list in the order of use in eight thousand random operations, with and without a time to live

capability cache/get  a value read, the entry counted as used, or only looked at
  heroes  cache.get, cache.peek, cache.contains
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    a read does not lengthen an entry's life, which runs from its last write

capability cache/remove  an entry taken out, every expired one forgotten, or all
  heroes  cache.remove, cache.expire, cache.clear
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Python's `lru_cache` offers `cache.clear` alone

capability cache/inspect  the entries by their last use, the next to be forgotten, how many are held
  heroes  cache.slots, cache.oldest_slot, cache.size
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Python's `cache_info` counts hits and misses, which the program counts as it asks; `cache_parameters` is `cache.capacity`

dropped traits  what an interface would have needed: a structure written for a debugger, hashed, ordered against another, dropped, converted
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  functools.cached_property
